#: ../../guide/fsm.rst:3
msgid "Finite State Machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/fsm.rst:5
msgid "The Finite State Machine (FSM) is aiorubi's mechanism for storing per-conversation *state* and *data* between updates. It is what turns a stateless ``new_message`` handler into a multi-step dialog: \"What is your name?\" → \"How old are you?\" → \"Done!\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/fsm.rst:10
msgid "If you have used aiogram 3.x, the FSM here works exactly the same way — same classes, same methods, same storage model. The only platform-specific detail is that all identifiers (``chat_id``, ``user_id``, ``bot_id``) are strings, because Rubika issues string ids."
msgstr ""

